{"text":"Approved tech stack pinned in STACK.md. Single source of truth for which tools/frameworks/versions this repo uses. Drives CLAUDE.md tech-stack section. Tool-agnostic context hub: any agent reading markdown picks up the constraints (Claude Code, Cursor, Continue, Aider, Codex CLI). Future Step 2/3 dependency additions must go through STACK.md amendment + bd decision record.","tags":["stack","context-hub","decisions","versions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-07","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard and any project that wants the same pattern"}
{"text":"Package manager: npm (not yarn or pnpm). Operator consensus 2026-05-07; secondary developer prefers npm; npm 10 workspaces are mature; pnpm/yarn-berry adoption is uneven. Lockfile is package-lock.json (committed).","tags":["npm","package-manager","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-07","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Node version manager: any tool that reads .nvmrc (nvm, fnm, volta, n). The repo pins .nvmrc 22.12.0; pick whichever manager the operator already has. Don't mix two on the same machine.","tags":["nvm","node-version","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-07","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Sessions-spike v4 write API: extend the existing packages/server (Fastify 5); do NOT add Go or a separate server. The monorepo is uniformly TypeScript with shared Zod types (@metaswarm-dashboard/types) and one vitest/coverage/eslint apparatus; a second language fragments the toolchain and breaks type-sharing for a handful of write endpoints. Go was floated by the operator and the choice explicitly delegated to the executor: evaluated and rejected.","tags":["stack","go-rejected","fastify","sessions-spike-v4","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-17","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Sessions-spike v4: the dashboard becomes read-WRITE, scoped strictly to its own datalake (METASWARM_DASHBOARD_DATA_DIR). Observed host repos stay strictly read-only — the zero-footprint-on-host-repos invariant is unchanged. Operator session ratings and snapshots are written into the datalake via Fastify endpoints. Supersedes the v3 read-only-SPA MVP stance; the SPA write-ban lint rule is re-scoped (SPA may POST only to the dashboard's own API).","tags":["architecture","read-write","datalake","sessions-spike-v4","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-17","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
